      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T16:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d rather not, because no matter the order of the two CLs (one for run_host_test, one for Makefile rules), the first CL will be broken.\nIf run_host_test is updated first, then it will fail when it gets to the tests that are currently being excluded (is_enabled_error, static_if_error, fpsensor, etc.)\nIf the Makefile rules are updated first, then generating code coverage will fail, because the proc.kill() in run_host_test will prevent any of the executables from generating code coverage output.\nIf these CLs were in different repos, I would have them Cq-Depend on each other. Either one is useless without the other.",
      "parentUuid": "06f7cb92_bc27c15d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
