      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a4369a6_c445bbf8",
        "filename": "util/run_host_test",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1331721
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-08T21:05:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m comfortable with leaving it as-is, because if this is running on a heavily-loaded system, 1 second may not be enough.\nThe tests exit very quickly, or they take 60 seconds and that tells you something is very wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "ebd881f2_286635ba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "a36816898aabe0ea7fd750b65053b1fea1c14daa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62b28522_c626d8a3",
        "filename": "util/run_host_test",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-08T21:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is code coverage going to run in the CQ as a part of src_test in the ebuild? That\u0027s where we had the timeout issues happening. I think 1 second is actually more than generous enough for all other scenarios.\n\nIf it\u0027s part of the CQ src_test phase, I\u0027d say we start at 5 seconds and bump it up if that\u0027s not enough.",
      "parentUuid": "0a4369a6_c445bbf8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "a36816898aabe0ea7fd750b65053b1fea1c14daa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
